{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291687-new-legacy-the-clockwork-knights","id":1291687,"title":"[New Legacy] The Clockwork Knights","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-24T19:26:49-08:00","id":1291687,"title":"[New Legacy] The Clockwork Knights","content":"Author's Note: The format for this Legacy is borrowed from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a> and the Form Blazing Sword spell was originally written by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a>. Feedback is greatly welcome.<br /> <br /> The Clockwork Knights take it upon themselves to wield knowledge and stoicism in the fight against all that would keep people afraid and ignorant. The culmination and icon of their creed is their namesake powered exoskeletons, which serve to both help them defend the innocent and inspire them to pursue greater discoveries.<br /> <br /> Origins<br /> Parentage: Moros, Adamantine Arrow<br /> Nicknames: Shields<br /> Background: Scientifically minded, brave and selfless individuals make up the ranks of this Legacy.<br /> Appearances: All of them possess at least decent physiques to properly withstand the regular use of their exoskeletons, which are often decorated with scars and medals that tell stories of their battles. It is not uncommon for clockwork to manifest in their Nimbus as well.<br /> <br /> Doctrine<br /> Prerequisites: Forces 2, Crafts 2, Science 2<br /> Initiation: The initiate must first prove that they are capable of upholding the Adamantine Arrow's principles even without their armor. After that, they must create an original design for their armor, and use it to neutralize a series of automatons in a simulation of an attack against an innocent population.<br /> <br /> Organization And History: The Shields trace their beginning to Ancient Greece, in a period when mythic monsters roamed the land largely unimpeded and many people did not have a way to fight back. Seeing this, the Adamantine Arrow of that time decided to intervene with both sword and books, not only protecting those in need but also teaching them about how to protect themselves. However, they were not necessarily a progressive group for quite some time, as they preserved most of the cultural biases of the era. They only managed to truly embody their ideals around the Age Of Enlightenment, but even then many local splinters of this Legacy based on differing technological and ethical notions still exist.<br /> <br /> Magic<br /> Ruling Arcanum: Forces<br /> Yantras: armaments (+1), symbols of honor and duty (+1), forges of various kinds (+2), trophies from battle (+2).<br /> Oblations: combat training, performing maintenance and experiments on your armor, explaining scientific ideas to a willing audience<br /> <br /> Attainments<br /> <br /> First: Guardian's Insight<br /> Prerequisite: Initiation<br /> Operating a powered exoskeleton with only the capacity of the human frame is clunky and extremely tiring. To remedy this, Shields learn to make the most of every movement. This works like Kinetic Efficiency and is cast as a Ritual, with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. Should the exoskeleton be larger than Size 5, ignore additional Size units equal to Forces dots x 2 for the purposes of negating the need for Advanced Scale. This Attainment is limited to the exoskeleton, but also grants Steadfast Condition on relevant rolls.<br /> Optional: Matter 1<br /> Shields must also learn the ins and outs of their exoskeletons. This works like Craftsman's Eye and is cast as a Ritual, with Reach assigned to Advanced Duration. This Attainment is limited to the exoskeleton but also grants Informed Condition on relevant rolls.<br /> <br /> Second: Unyielding Stride<br /> Prerequisite: Forces 2, One of the Prerequisite Skills At 3<br /> Shields often venture into places with hazards that can destroy a basic exoskeleton. To deal with this, they learn to enhance the protection of the exoskeleton against the elements. This works like Environmental Shield, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting. This Attainment only applies when wearing the exoskeleton, but also protects against direct damage.<br /> Optional: Matter 2<br /> Shields commonly interact with the fallout of dangerous or reckless use of chemicals and learn to handle said chemicals safely. This works like Alchemist's Touch, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting. This Attainment only applies when wearing the exoskeleton, but the Mage is shielded against all harsh chemicals. It also applies an active and permanent Clash of Wills using Gnosis + Matter against supernatural attempts at affecting the exoskeleton. The Mage achieves automatic Successes equal to Matter dots.<br /> <br /> Third: Ready For Anything<br /> Prerequisite: Forces 3, Both of the Prerequisite Skills At 3<br /> Shields know that sometimes being quick is not enough, one must act with the swiftness of lightning. This works like Velocity Control, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting. Should the exoskeleton be larger than Size 5, ignore additional Size units equal to Forces dots x 2 for the purposes of negating the need for Advanced Scale. This is limited to the exoskeleton, but actions that benefit from the Attainment achieve automatic Successes equal to Forces dots.<br /> Optional: Matter 3<br /> Shields also know that no plan survives contact with the enemy, but that it always pays to have backup plans. This works like Wonderful Machine, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting. This Attainment is limited to the exoskeleton, but any use of the resulting machines gains an Equipment Bonus equal to Matter dots.<br /> <br /> Fourth: Heroic Arsenal<br /> Prerequisite: Forces 4, One of the Prerequisite Skills at 4 and the other at 3<br /> Shields are never unarmed, the elements themselves serve as their weapons. This works like Form Blazing Sword (see below), with Reach assigned to Instant Casting and maintaining Potency with additional strikes. As an exception to the general workings of the Legacy, this Attainment may be used without the exoskeleton. But should the Mage be wearing the exoskeleton regardless, he may apply the Down And Dirty Combat rules, achieving automatic Successes equal to Forces dots.<br /> Optional: Matter 4<br /> Shields do not fear failure, for they can push the exoskeleton to it limits and beyond. This works like Crucible, with Reach Assigned to Instant Casting and gaining Rote Quality. This is limited to the exoskeleton, but add Matter dots to Initiative and Defense as well.<br /> <br /> Form Blazing Sword (Forces \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Crafts, Intimidation, Occult<br /> The Mage shapes and contains a source of energy into a melee weapon of elemental force. A campfire becomes a blade of flame, a musical performance becomes a hammer of sound, or beams of sunlight become spears. The weapon has a Lethal Damage Bonus equal to Potency, or General Armor equal to Potency if it is a shield. Potency may be divided among multiple armaments. Each impact that is given or received reduces the remaining Potency by one as the elemental force dissipates. The Mage is not harmed by merely holding the weapon, and it may be used with any applicable Fighting Styles.<br /> +1 Reach: Strikes do not reduce Potency.<br /> +1 Reach: As a reflexive action the Mage may reconfigure the weapon into another form, but maintains the type of elemental force.<br /> <br /> Fifth: Heart Of Lightning And Fire<br /> Prerequisite: Forces 5, Both of the Prerequisite Skills at 4<br /> Shields who reach the this level of power need not worry about their exoskeletons ever running out of energy. This works like Transform Energy, with Reach Assigned to Instant Casting and Advanced Scale. This is limited to powering the exoskeleton, but should the Mage need to perform a Clash Of Wills, he achieves automatic Successes equal to Forces dots.<br /> Optional: Matter 5<br /> Shields who have conquered the pinnacle of their Legacy have become one with their exoskeleton. This Attainment is treated as if it was a combination of Transubstantiation + Shaping + Shrink And Grow, but it needs no roll and is done reflexively. Effectively, the Mage may disguise his exoskeleton as mundane clothing, a suitcase or a similar belonging, which returns to the active form at will. Furthermore, the Mage always knows the approximate direction and distance of the exoskeleton and has a precise understanding of its overall state. Lastly, he may operate it as if casting Remote Control, but no roll is needed and it is done reflexively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-25-2019, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T19:57:49-08:00","id":1291699,"title":"","content":"T